8|0@Nootropics^1439916548#cu77btv:PragmaticPulp$:Ashwagandha extract has enough mild-to-moderate effects on several hormone systems (in murine models at least) that I would recommend not taking it at higher doses. Once you start taking larger doses of these extracts, you end up with a lot of various compounds floating around in your blood. It's not like taking a larger dosage of a pure prescription medication that contains only a single, highly active ingredient. I'd file this firmly under the "bad idea with little to no possible upside" category. Avoid.
