2|0@Nootropics^1439951577#cu7tjwo:Vulpyne$:Is 2g even what would be considered a mega dose? *The lowest effective dose for acute usage of ashwagandha, and perhaps the most cost-effective dose, is 300-500mg.* ***The optimal dose is 6,000mg a day usually divided into three doses (2,000mg)*** *and while 300-500mg is effective for most situations a lower dose of 50-100mg can be seen as effective in few instances such as reducing the immunosuppression seen with stress and augmenting anxiolytic (anxiety reducing agents).* — http://examine.com/supplements/ashwagandha/ I believe that's talking about dry ~~root~~ (*edit:*) leaves though: *Unless otherwise standardized to a certain percentage, the amount of active Withanolide A (seen as the primary ingredient) and Withaferin-A are 1% of dry weight of the leaves (with negligible content in the roots) of Withania Somnifera.* — http://examine.com/supplements/ashwagandha/#summary1 If my math is correct, the optimal dose for 2.5% Withanolide A would be 2.4g according to Examine. ***Disclaimer***: This isn't medical advice. Examine could be wrong. I could be wrong. My math could be all crazy. 
